00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.930 align:start position:0%
the witness is one of the most  challenging games I've ever played  during my playthrough I experience  confusion uncertainty and mental  exhaustion as I tried to understand this  game's intricacies the witness makes few  attempts at hand-holding opting instead  to convey its mechanics and subtle  cryptic ways as you struggle to make  sense of it all but when you do persist  frustration gives way to gratification  this is what makes the witness so  special  unlike many puzzle games it doesn't just  make you feel intelligent it begins on  the assumption that you are intelligent  the witness unfolds on an unnamed Island  within a vast sea this island comprises  a patchwork pattern of Earth's biomes  from a snow-capped Mountain down to a  barren desert scattered throughout these  habitats are square panels each covered  in mazes of varying complexity this here  is the foundation of the witness's  gameplay you guide a glowing line  through each maze and continue from  there most panels unlock subsequent  puzzles but some open doors maneuver  platforms or even activate power sources  what's remarkable is how the witness  communicates it to nuances early panels  are easy as 'king you to guide the line  from point A to B on simple grids after  some time though new symbols and colors  and shapes appear each conveying their  own new rules and there are never overt  instructions as to how these rules work  you learn them on your own through  intuition and logical reasoning it's  also impressive how diverse the puzzles  are and how the witness manages keep  mazes engaging over the course of 25  hours or more it's more impressive when  the witness reveals that its world and  the puzzles therein aren't exactly  separate sometimes they bleed together  what's more the island is open from the  start leaving you free to wander between  its puzzles and locales this is a vital  part to the witness's structure each  area houses a different motif among its  panels based around a certain symbol or  clue in its mazes if the increasing  difficulty of one areas puzzles becomes  too high you can put it down cross the  island and learn a new rule entirely in  many cases the knowledge you acquire  elsewhere helps you better understand  the puzzle you just put down  the witness isn't open-world just for  the sake of exploration if structure  encourages learning at your own pace and  to discuss any of these puzzle solutions  would mean spoiling the revelations that  await you the witness introduces new  ideas with elegance never stating the  rules outright never showing its full  hand but giving you just enough context  and just enough of a push to make the  final leap yourself and after completing  enough of the puzzles bigger overarching  objectives emerge as it does with  various panels the witness communicates  your goals with a whisper offering  nudges in one direction or another as  you make meaningful connections between  disparate parts of the island some of  the puzzles though lack what makes the  rest so good instead of leaning on for  Thought and careful observation several  panels exist to test your dexterity it's  one thing when these examples rest in  optional areas off the beaten path but  it's all the more frustrating when one  of them impedes you from reaching an  important area on the island because of  the solitude of this island in the  various ways its mysteries can unfold  there's not really a linear series of  events but there is a story through  audio logs and other media I won't spoil  here the witness quotes the observations  and experiences of real-life physicists  astronauts psychologists and explorers  each trying to figure out the world  around them and that's what the witness  is about gaining knowledge and using it  intelligently to make sense of the  island and it's gorgeous but exotic  environments the witness moulds its  world puzzles and themes into such a  cohesive whole that if we look hard  enough  we'll keep finding new ways to perceive  it over and over and over again there  are still things in the witness I can't  make sense of some clues I might never  notice and some puzzles I might never  solve but the hints are there it might  not all make sense at first but that's  okay because I'm always learning
 

